---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Signup from '../components/Signup.astro';
import ExecCTA from '../components/ExecCTA.astro';
import Perceptron from '../components/Perceptron.astro';
---
<Base>
  <section class="hero">
    <div class="wrap hero__grid">
      <div class="hero__text">
        <h1>NU AI Safety</h1>
        <p class="tagline">AI safety and interpretability at Northeastern.</p>
        <p>
          We are a student-led group preparing Northeastern students to help align and govern
          advanced AI systems. We will run technical and policy fellowships, host talks from
          researchers, and support student research.
        </p>
        <div class="actions">
          <Signup />
          <ExecCTA />
        </div>
        <p class="hero__more">
          <a class="arrow" href="/about"><span>What we are planning to do</span></a>
        </p>
      </div>
      <figure class="hero__art">
        <Perceptron />
        <figcaption>
          Organization of a perceptron, after Rosenblatt, 1958. Red marks the cells active for
          the input, and the response unit that fires as a result.
        </figcaption>
      </figure>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="band band--wash" aria-labelledby="what">
    <div class="wrap">
      <h2 id="what" class="sr-only-heading">What we are planning to do</h2>
      <div class="grid grid--3">
        <div class="block">
          <h3>Fellowships</h3>
          <span class="meta">About 90 minutes a week</span>
          <p>
            Weekly reading groups on the technical and policy sides of AI safety, from the
            fundamentals to current research.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="block">
          <h3>Guest talks</h3>
          <span class="meta">On campus</span>
          <p>
            Talks from researchers in AI safety and interpretability.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="block">
          <h3>Research</h3>
          <span class="meta">Members’ own projects</span>
          <p>
            Support for members pursuing their own AI safety research, with feedback and
            collaboration from other members.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="band" aria-labelledby="whofor">
    <div class="wrap prose">
      <h2 id="whofor">Who this is for</h2>
      <p>
        AI safety is not only a machine learning problem. It runs through policy, security,
        biology, law and psychology, and it needs people who are good at those things. A room
        that is only engineers will miss things.
      </p>
      <p>
        You do not need machine learning experience, a CS degree, or any prior knowledge of AI
        safety. If the groups that already exist feel like they are for people who know all this
        already, that is exactly the gap we are built for.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="band band--wash" aria-labelledby="new">
    <div class="wrap">
      <h2 id="new">We are new</h2>
      <div class="callout">
        <p>
          Five people, a faculty researcher who agreed to help, and no events yet. If you join
          now you are shaping what this is rather than attending something finished.
        </p>
      </div>
      <p>
        We are not doing it alone. We are coordinating with BU AI Safety, and Harvard AISST and
        MIT MAIA have both offered help.
      </p>
      <div class="actions">
        <Signup />
        <ExecCTA />
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  /* The section needs a heading for the outline; the three blocks carry the meaning. */
  .sr-only-heading {
    position: absolute;
    width: 1px; height: 1px;
    padding: 0; margin: -1px;
    overflow: hidden;
    clip-path: inset(50%);
    white-space: nowrap;
  }
</style>
